    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile anchored by **Trea Turner** (75.08) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.50). **Trea Turner** remains our premier start; his combination of the leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Sandy Alcantara allows him to leverage his elite speed, a critical component for our 5x5 Roto standing. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a strong tailwind and a soft matchup against Sean Sullivan. While his dynamic platoon split is naturally negative, the combination of the #1 spot and the favorable wind conditions elevates his efficiency score well into the elite tier, making him a cornerstone of today's production strategy.\n\nOur decision-making process leaned heavily into platoon advantages and park factors. **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.22) both received significant boosts due to high-value SP skill matchups, with **Kazuma Okamoto** particularly poised to exploit the 4.88 xERA of Jake Bennett. The most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (51.52), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Carson Benge** maintains a strong baseline, the combination of an unfavorable lefty-on-lefty matchup and a wind-in warning at the stadium ultimately capped his upside compared to the higher efficiency ratings of **Colt Keith** and **Casey Schmitt**.\n\nRisk mitigation remains a primary focus, as several rostered players\u2014including **Gary Sanchez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich**\u2014remain \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled these lineups based on historical trends, any deviation in the batting order could necessitate a late-day assessment. Furthermore, while we are confident in **Christian Yelich** (63.23), we are mindful that his matchup against Gavin Williams presents a challenge; his score is buoyed by his leadoff position and a favorable dynamic platoon split. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains sidelined in the minors, while ensuring that the rest of our depth, including **Rece Hinds**, **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, are kept in reserve should injury or late-scratch scenarios arise.",
